From f96f3f91032d1630104c635e525b7c1e3316ec7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aeron-Aeron <aeronrules2@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 14:05:32 +0545
Subject: [PATCH] libutils: binder: disable CallStack for MiuiCamera lag fix

MiuiCamera lags ~3.5s on lens/mode switch because
libmialgoengine.so destroys ~170 sp<MiaNode> objects per session
teardown. Without ANDROID_UTILS_CALLSTACK_ENABLED=0, each
destruction triggers a full 50-frame native stack unwind via
RefBase — ~20ms per call — gating MIADestroySession.

Adding the flag to libutils_binder_impl_defaults_nodeps_no_apex
kills the stack dump while keeping the one-line warning.
switch_prefix_camera_setup drops from ~3500ms to under 500ms.

Signed-off-by: Aeron-Aeron <aeronrules2@gmail.com>
---
 libutils/binder/Android.bp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/libutils/binder/Android.bp b/libutils/binder/Android.bp
index f6a777e..13e7bd1 100644
--- a/libutils/binder/Android.bp
+++ b/libutils/binder/Android.bp
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@ cc_defaults {
         "-Winvalid-offsetof",
         "-Wsequence-point",
         "-Wzero-as-null-pointer-constant",
+        "-DANDROID_UTILS_CALLSTACK_ENABLED=0",
     ],
 
     afdo: true,
